## For yoga, dance and movement

A light-filled practice space with exposed timber roof trusses, a bank of large windows looking out to the trees and playground, and a warm parquet floor at its centre. Ideal for instructors looking for a regular slot, and for individual practitioners or small groups wanting somewhere consistent to work.

The central parquet section (4.3m × 4.7m) provides a warm, bare-wood surface for mat work, flow practices and barefoot movement. A full-length wall-mounted barre runs along one side of the room - good for ballet, barre classes, contemporary dance, yoga warm-ups and balance work. When chairs are cleared and stored in the on-site furniture bay, the full room opens to approximately 75 m² of clear floor.

The vaulted ceiling gives full headroom for standing sequences, inversions and aerial work.

**Ideal for:** weekly classes, workshops, small retreats, teacher-led private sessions, one-to-one tuition, ballet and barre classes.

---

## For martial arts

A clear, uncluttered space with the dimensions and ceiling height for serious training. The room runs to 11 metres in length and the high vaulted ceiling gives full headroom for kicks, jumps and weapons forms.

**Ideal for:** karate, taekwondo, jiu-jitsu, judo, kickboxing, tai chi, qigong, capoeira and other martial and movement disciplines.

![The studio cleared for martial arts training](/images/facilities/large-room/large-room-3.jpeg)

---

## For meetings, workshops and events

The room seats **70 theatre-style** using the on-site chairs. For cabaret or workshop layouts, six 80×80cm square tables are available alongside two larger tables - a 278×183cm banquet table and a 110×122cm table. Additional furniture can be borrowed from the adjoining Lounge when it's free.

One end of the room has a curtained presentation area - a useful focal point for talks, demonstrations or performance. Note: there's no screen or projector on site, so please bring your own if needed.

**Ideal for:** birthday parties, community meetings, workshops, training days, talks, club AGMs, hobby groups and one-off events.

![The studio set up theatre-style with 70 chairs](/images/facilities/large-room/large-room-with-chairs.jpeg)

---

## The wider Meadowbrook site

The studio sits within the broader Meadowbrook facility. On-site sauna access is available separately, and peaceful walking trails run alongside the brook - making this a particularly good base for wellness practitioners who want to offer their guests something beyond the session itself.

[Visit The Somewhere Sauna](/facilities/somewhere-sauna) · [Explore the brook and woodland](/facilities/woodland-and-brook)

---

## ⚠ Please note: noise from the bar below

The studio sits above Things happen here (bar). There can occasionally be sound bleed from events held downstairs or outside - something worth knowing about if you're planning a quiet or sound-sensitive session such as meditation, a sound bath or restorative yoga.

Most daytime and early-evening sessions are unaffected. Larger events and live music tend to be on weekend evenings. We recommend checking the events calendar before booking.

[View upcoming events at Things Happen Here](https://thingshappenhere.co.uk/whats-on/)

---

## Frequently asked questions

**Can I book the studio for a regular weekly class?**
Yes - we welcome recurring bookings. [email bookings@meadowbrookdartington.org](mailto:bookings@meadowbrookdartington.org) if you want to view the room, or discuss arrangements. The form below can be used to make repeating bookings.

**Is there a sound system?**
No - please bring your own speaker. The room has power sockets throughout.

**Is there parking?**
Yes, parking is available on site.

**Is the studio accessible?**
Access to the studio is via a flight of stairs - it is not currently step-free. Please [get in touch](/contact) if you have questions about access.

**Tidy up**
Please ensure the studio is left in a clean and orderly state after use. There is a hoover in the cupboard beside the room.